Original commit body from 70a430a3e01f9a95ccabb4c79d55730092a0aef0:

`hypergumbo build-grammars` (and the grammars step of `add-extras`)
could not work from a pip/pipx install. The Lean, Wolfram and Circom C
sources lived in a repo-root `vendor/`, found as
`Path(__file__).parents[4] / "vendor"`; the hypergumbo-core wheel packages
only `src/hypergumbo_core`, so from an install that path resolved to
`<venv>/vendor` and all three grammars failed (exit 1). Reproduced from
fresh venvs built from the release workflow's `python -m build` wheels.

Move the tree to `hypergumbo_core/vendor/` (package data, resolved beside
the module), so one path serves source checkout, editable install, sdist
and wheel. Each grammar's MIT LICENSE and UPSTREAM pin ship with it.
Compressed wheel grows 2,703,208 -> 3,419,413 bytes (+0.7 MB).

The missing-source error now names the looked-up path and tells an
installed user to reinstall hypergumbo-core, instead of pointing at a doc
that exists only in a source checkout; it is now tested (no pragma).
scripts/build-source-grammars, docs/grammars/vendor-sync.md, the I/O
allowlist target text, README command table (root + meta copy), spec and
CHANGELOG follow.

Refs INV-bazoz-jurog-jihav-butod-pabih-tobob-vofor-susug

